Recompiler: div.s by zero (or by a denormal) gives the largest finite number, not an infinity.

What it fixes: the emitted text tested `ft == 0.0f`, set a flag bit the console does not have (0x100000) and wrote
copysignf(INFINITY, fs * 0.0f), which is a NaN when fs is zero. The console has no infinities and no NaNs: the reference
emulator's interpreter (third_party/pcsx2/pcsx2/FPU.cpp, DIV_S and checkDivideByZero, :107 and DIV_S below it) gives the largest
finite number with the sign of the operands when the divisor's exponent field is zero (a denormal counts as zero), sets
D|SD in FCR31 (I|SI when the dividend is zero too) and does not touch the destination otherwise. The emitted text now does that
with bit operations on the two registers; any other divisor uses the host's division, which under the game's mode (round
toward zero, flush-to-zero, denormals-are-zero) is the console's.

How it was verified: tests/conformance family "fpu", div.s: 735 cases differed before (zero, denormal and normal divisors with
dividends of every class) and 411 after, all of them with an operand whose exponent field is all ones (not clamped: see
journal 025, piece 5). The infinity that a division by zero used to put in a register fed every later operation on it; this
removes that source. 1,981 div.s sites in the game. A division by zero can happen in a fight (a length that is zero, a
normalisation of a null vector).

Original work for this repository (no code from another project).

diff --git a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/fpu_translator.cpp b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/fpu_translator.cpp
--- a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/fpu_translator.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/fpu_translator.cpp
@@ -53,10 +53,15 @@
             case COP1_S_MUL:
                 return fmt::format("ctx->f[{}] = FPU_MUL_S(ctx->f[{}], ctx->f[{}]);", fd, fs, ft);
             case COP1_S_DIV:
-                return fmt::format("if (ctx->f[{}] == 0.0f) {{ ctx->fcr31 |= 0x100000; /* DZ flag */ "
-                                   "ctx->f[{}] = copysignf(INFINITY, ctx->f[{}] * 0.0f); }} "
-                                   "else ctx->f[{}] = ctx->f[{}] / ctx->f[{}];",
-                                   ft, fd, fs, fd, fs, ft);
+                // The console has no infinities: a divisor with exponent 0 (zero, or a denormal, which does not exist) gives the
+                // largest finite number with the sign of the operands and sets D|SD (I|SI when the dividend is zero too)
+                // (FPU.cpp: DIV_S, checkDivideByZero). Any other divisor: the host's division, which under the game's
+                // round-toward-zero mode is the console's.
+                return fmt::format("{{ uint32_t a_, b_; std::memcpy(&a_, &ctx->f[{}], sizeof(a_)); std::memcpy(&b_, &ctx->f[{}], sizeof(b_)); "
+                                   "if ((b_ & 0x7F800000u) == 0) {{ ctx->fcr31 |= ((a_ & 0x7F800000u) == 0) ? 0x20040u : 0x10020u; "
+                                   "uint32_t r_ = ((a_ ^ b_) & 0x80000000u) | 0x7F7FFFFFu; std::memcpy(&ctx->f[{}], &r_, sizeof(r_)); }} "
+                                   "else ctx->f[{}] = ctx->f[{}] / ctx->f[{}]; }}",
+                                   fs, ft, fd, fd, fs, ft);
             case COP1_S_SQRT:
                 // R5900: SQRT.S fd, ft takes its source from ft (the fs field is 0).
                 // Negative inputs use the magnitude (PCSX2 FPU.cpp SQRT_S).
